  "description": "ZEZYIO crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C53 H64 Dy6 N12 O26,C1 H4 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.343-4.609 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.66-158.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6L4(μ4-O)(NO3)4(CH3OH)]·CH3OH (C54H68Dy6N12O27; CCDC C53H64Dy6N12O26·CH4O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
